{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLLFtaZ9DrkAMfXsroFX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fixed the bug: `bug.apart(t)` now returns `-a*t + a/2 - a/(2*(2*t - 1))` instead of `-a*t`. Five tests in `sympy/polys` fail, but the same five fail without my change, so this change doesn't cause them.\n\n**Cause:** `apart` divides polynomials with coefficients that can depend on `a`. To do that, it switches to fractions in `a` (`ZZ(a)`), divides, then converts the result back to plain polynomials in `a` (`ZZ[a]`). That conversion back is in `PolynomialRing.from_FractionField` (`sympy/polys/domains/polynomialring.py:105`). For a fraction like `a/2`, it divided with integer-only arithmetic, which silently threw away any term that didn't divide exactly. So `a/2` became `0` instead of failing. Because the conversion \"succeeded\", `Poly.div` handed back the wrong quotient `-a*t` and remainder `0`, and `apart` returned `-a*t`.\n\n**Fix:** the conversion now divides the numerator by the denominator and checks the remainder. It only converts when the remainder is zero. Otherwise it returns `None`, which tells the caller the value can't be expressed in `ZZ[a]`, so `div` keeps the result as fractions. The change is three lines in that one function.\n\n**Tests:** I ran `sympy/polys` with and without the change, and the same five tests fail both times:\n- `test_fields.py::test_FracElement___call__`\n- `test_partfrac.py::test_noncommutative_pseudomultivariate`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_factor_noeval`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_poly_matching_consistency`\n- `test_polytools.py::test_issue_5786`\n\nI didn't look into why they fail."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1309,"cache_read_input_tokens":30052,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1309},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"51b1182b-ae17-46d5-88d4-7f7245a56956","uuid":"c983b3f6-c001-43ea-8d5a-5ab7056119d8","timestamp":"2026-11-23T18:28:20.215Z","request_id":"req_011ChLLFtRsho4UU5My68csk"}
